William Brodersen User Stories:
1. As a user, I want the app to work the same after backend changes, So that I experience no regressions
- [] Navigation works
- [] User pages load correctly
- [] Photo views display properly
- [] No UI breaks occur after migration
2. As a user, I want to see a list of users in the sidebar, so that I can navigate between profiles
-[] Endpoint returns _id, first_name, last_name
-[] Data is fetched from MongoDB
-[] Response format matches UI needs
3. As a user, I want to view detailed information about a user, So that I can learn more about them
-[] Return full user details (_id, name, location, description, occupation)
-[] Invalid IDs return HTTP 400 with message
-[] Data comes from MongoDB


Harrison Syfert User Stories:
4. As a user, I want the backend to fetch data from MongoDB instead of static models, so that the app uses real database data
-[] No usage of models.photoApp.js remains
-[] Data is retrieved using Mongoose schemas
-[] Server connects successfully to MongoDB
-[] All routes return database-backed responses
5. As a user, I want the /user/list API to return minimal user data, so that the sidebar loads quickly
-[] Returns only _id, first_name, last_name
-[] Data is fetched from MongoDB Users collection
-[] Response is formatted as an array
-[] Handles empty or missing users gracefully
6. As a user, I want the /user/:id API to return detailed user information, so that I can view a user profile
-[] Returns _id, first_name, last_name, location, description, occupation
-[] Valid user IDs return correct data
-[] Invalid IDs return HTTP 400 with message
-[] Data is retrieved using Mongoose
